{"title":"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following describes the largest subset of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> within the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece27ba559bd93cdf2416aa0f88fc8d7d85e5791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> for which\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9b2c0b1c3b4bd2cd0535f1bcd6552a064d603ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(x+y)\\leq \\sin(x)+\\sin(y)\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"18\" />for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, inclusive?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9d860ad26fc54f94a8a9c675591f704c525ee94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } y=0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 0\\leq y\\leq \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 0\\leq y\\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 0\\leq y\\leq \\frac{3\\pi}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 0\\leq y\\leq \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"684\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a151f5b93ce5735f72cdd79c46051f52b9d820d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> sine is nonnegative; thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e32d38fb72f609bfde37807498393750ab12299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x + y) = \\sin x \\cos y + \\sin y \\cos x \\le \\sin x + \\sin y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"393\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/447a91e1512333fc639da02e03bf52a259f38101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y \\in [0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" /> and equality only occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8133b5800b18e2848c082f5d3f7c2c9a6b75cc59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x = \\cos y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" />, which is cosine's maximum value. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0ef915acbcedcac7bbc707b87b4e7f8f9d6569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 0\\le y\\le \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"123\" height=\"28\" />. (CantonMathGuy)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expanding, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a916ee8c05e199ecfa5fb02e05d7868542a433.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos y \\sin x + \\cos x \\sin y \\le \\sin x + \\sin y\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"15\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f5735fa897775c9de24396a5e7708b2a41ae92d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin x =a \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b37f8d2e03f225e1ea031be774f9bd6fefb0246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin y = b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/81993ddeff536aa854fdcff82c41fd83230cb359.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(\\cos y)a+(\\cos x)b \\le a+b\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"18\" /> Comparing coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> gives a clear solution: both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c942a316ee4efd35e46023dcf3256ef90e9814db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/f/11f986c49f29d7a2ed4c28cab7319fa2ee3ee978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x$\" width=\"37\" height=\"8\" /> are less than or equal to one, so the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> on the left are less than on the right. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d5886e00dedd073f57500e340a0eec42783ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, that means that this equality is always satisfied over this interval, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0ef915acbcedcac7bbc707b87b4e7f8f9d6569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 0\\le y\\le \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"123\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/4/184911dcfe7d6e007429d3197c2daaef8c115f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x+\\pi) \\le \\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />. Note that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081bf0417da2140657aad909a14ca6c3ff8b77d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> is always nonnegative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da2564b9cbb4ce6887ccb9d48d942f84c4da5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(x+\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> is always nonpositive. So, the inequality holds true when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/1/2916ed0f56f21d142a58d28c6aab6e5d27160a4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" />. The only interval that contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> in the answer choices is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0ef915acbcedcac7bbc707b87b4e7f8f9d6569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 0\\le y\\le \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"123\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 4 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> there is equality and nowhere else because the angle is not being rotated enough. We can just try all the subset of values from the answer choices to try out preferably the largest value for each subset that works as they've special trig values and are the upper bound for the set with values of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> interval.\n</p><p>From this we notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has the largest bound from the answer choices that works. Hence our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n~Batmanstark\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite it as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a916ee8c05e199ecfa5fb02e05d7868542a433.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos y \\sin x + \\cos x \\sin y \\le \\sin x + \\sin y\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"15\" /> then move the terms such that it appears as this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b59330201312f8a53c98ca605cc4755ab7f5aef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin x (\\cos y -1) \\le \\sin y (1- \\cos x)\\]\" width=\"258\" height=\"18\" /> We know that on the interval of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a151f5b93ce5735f72cdd79c46051f52b9d820d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, \\pi]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/b/1dbe519076aee7a5bd68b4eb7484e5a8b7d989ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le (1-\\cos x)\\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24fd05ca589ea5d6b621623c077f691c8a5991f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le \\sin y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, such that the whole thing on the right hand side is always greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. On the left hand side, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c9802d4902c02ed128e3b1d2729be9d1a4e50d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> and we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/f/33fb0673f94f663cff551db189e61ccc6b231fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\cos y -1)\\le 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />, which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773579dbb5661d580648a8b7c1bc345bf9197d5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{0\\le y\\le \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"91\" height=\"29\" /> satisfies. \n~azure123456\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sum-to-product_identities\" title=\"Sum-to-product identities\">Sum-to-product identities</a>, the inequality simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/251a0afe86a180d87ac24ced07e7fbc2b82687f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{x-y}{2}\\right)\\ge\\cos\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"225\" height=\"45\" />. (This manipulation requires dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69d18cd33ab4903f2ce4af7a7a7db575917c0e5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\left(\\frac{x+y}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"100\" height=\"45\" />, but this value is always positive since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f51997456ddc49869d1b4d6c63f9d56ac95807e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y}{2}\\le\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"37\" /> for all given values, so we do not have to flip the sign of the inequality.) This can be interpreted as choosing a value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081b7402c500e0dc0f4b00ce6ab1df9673f1d941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{2}\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"35\" />, making this value the new center of the cosine graph in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-direction, and taking both points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/fee416dbd9373ac22a4fa8b225d583e02ce8153a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{2}\\in\\left[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"35\" /> distance from the center. By looking at the graph, we find that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-values, the change in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> always makes it so that the value left of the center is greater than the value right of the center, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0ef915acbcedcac7bbc707b87b4e7f8f9d6569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 0\\le y\\le \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"123\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~eevee9406 (look at the graph if you don't understand)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A\">2018 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2018 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirec